# The template repository's own, distinct from template/.gitattributes.jinja,
# which is the one rendered into a repository.
#
# copier copies a file without a .jinja suffix byte for byte, so the line
# endings in this working tree are the ones a rendered repository receives.
# With core.autocrlf true, which is the Windows default, a checkout here turns
# every plain .yml into CRLF and the rendered repository then fails its own
# yamllint with "wrong new line character: expected \n" on twenty files. A
# render on macOS passed, so the fault appeared on one platform only.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree rather than the index alone, which is what
# autocrlf would otherwise override. A file jinja renders is unaffected either
# way, since jinja writes the output itself.
* text=auto eol=lf
